# Frontend UI Standards

## Data Fetching & State Boundaries
- Components MUST NOT call `fetch` or `axios` directly. Wrap all HTTP endpoints in custom React Query hooks (`useQuery`, `useMutation`).
- Server State: Owned exclusively by React Query Cache (`invalidateQueries` on successful mutations).
- Local UI State: Managed via React `useState` / `useReducer`.

## HITL Dashboard Requirements
- Display pending access requests with AI recommendation, confidence score, and policy chunk citations.
- Clearly present current user entitlements fetched from Postgres alongside target entitlement details.
- Provide explicit "Approve", "Deny", and "Manual Override" controls.
